            <ArticleTitle>[The electrocardiogram of the long-lived. Observations gathered from a study of 190 subjects over 80].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1019-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Authors have examined the ECG of 190 older than 80 patients. The 5,78% have resulted &quot;normal&quot; and the 12,10% &quot;border-line&quot;; the disturbances of the excitability (67,36%) have been more than those of the conduction (31,04%) among which the Left Anterior Emi-block have been important (12,10%). The myocardial infarction has been infrequent (7,89%) where the Left Ventricular Hypertrophia has been the 20%; the left deviation of the ventricular complexes has represented the 61,57%, the synusal rhythm the 85,26%, the normal rate has been present in 79,47% of the cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
